  "worked_solution": "To find the length of Mary's plot of land, we need to factor the expression ${x}^{2}-25.$\n\nFirst, we write the expression as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-25={x}^{2}-{5}^{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor the expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-25=(x+5)(x-5)\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the length of the plot must be $x-5$ yards.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14162885/assets/1d05c236e65fb4011152735b09dd7668bd6a36b119319a95ec1f3064bd13db4a.png)",
